    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0127" n="1195" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">110.11 DU/9–1554</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Prime Minister Mendès-France
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d55-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-09-15">September 15,
                        1954</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: This is just a brief
                    note to let you know that I plan to make a quick visit to London and Bonn
                    Thursday and <pb facs="0128" n="1196" xml:id="pg1196"/> Friday. I regret that
                    time is so short because it will not permit me to stop over in Paris to talk
                    with you much as I would like to do so. However I hope that we will have this
                    opportunity very shortly when we meet either in London or in New York at the
                    UN.</p>
                <p>Until then, with best wishes,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d55-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foster Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d55-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d55-f1-content">
                <p>The source text, drafted by Merchant, was transmitted to the Embassy in Paris in
                    niact telegram 954 of Sept. 15 with instructions that it be delivered to
                    Mendès-France as a personal message.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d55-f2" n="2" xml:id="d55-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 1098 from Paris, Sept. 15, Ambassador Dillon informed the Department
                    of State that the message was delivered and that the effect of omitting Paris
                    from the Secretary’s itinerary “will be salutatory” (110.11 DU/9–1554).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
